    "law": "Snell's law at entry gives n_external sin(theta) = n_core sin(r). Total internal reflection at the core-cladding boundary requires cos(r) >= n_cladding/n_core in the limiting-angle convention. Thus theta_max = asin(sqrt(n_core^2 - n_cladding^2)/n_external). The numerical aperture is sqrt(1.5^2 - 1.44^2) = 0.42.",
